34,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data reveals a significant imbalance. Only two people use the room frequently, yet the evidence of eating at desks suggests the room isn't serving its purpose. We are dealing with a lack of structure and misplaced habits.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we are missing more than just structure. I've found that our only unplanned interactions happen by the printer, and difficult conversations are happening in public, leaving people isolated and silent for weeks afterward.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"And here's the kicker: we're paying for outside rooms because this one is a disaster, yet facilities are barely called. That means we're either ignoring the mess or wasting hours fixing things ourselves. Who's actually doing that work?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, stop worrying about who's scrubbing the floors. We've spent 68,000 yen on external rentals because this room is inadequate. We're paying for a space we already have, which is a textbook waste of capital.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is clear that our sanctuary has become a source of stress. The walls are thin, allowing every word to drift into our workspace, and the crumbs at our desks show we have abandoned the room for convenience.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the financial waste is a symptom of the lack of a system. If the room had a defined purpose and a fair usage agreement, we wouldn't be paying for external rentals or eating at our desks.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, a system for cleaning is helpful, but we also need a system for our humanity. If we have no private place for difficult words, we will remain strangers despite the rules.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, humanity is great, but it doesn't scrub the bins. If we're paying for outside rooms, it's because this one is a failure. I'm tired of the hidden labor that keeps this place barely functioning.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, a ""system"" doesn't pay the bills. We have concrete quotes for fit-outs: 141,000 for a professional setup or 96,000 for a kitchen. We need to decide which investment actually stops the bleeding of external rental costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Money is a tool, but peace is the goal. If we build a kitchen but the walls remain thin, we only invite more noise and mess into our sanctuary. We must prioritize a space that offers true quiet.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the kitchen fit-out might stop the desk crumbs, but it doesn't solve the usage imbalance. We need a purpose that justifies the investment and ensures the room is used fairly, not just as a place to eat.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, I agree. A kitchen solves a physical problem, but it doesn't solve the emotional distance between us. We need a space that encourages genuine connection and provides privacy for the conversations we are currently avoiding.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, you're talking about ""connection,"" but I'm talking about the actual toll on us. If we just add a kitchen, who's managing the upkeep? I don't want another ""solution"" that just adds more chores to our day.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're thinking like a janitor, not a professional. The real toll is the inefficiency. We're paying for external rooms because we lack a proper meeting space. A professional fit-out is a one-time cost that eliminates recurring waste.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Shunichi, efficiency is a hollow victory if it comes at the cost of our serenity. A professional room is useless if the walls still whisper every secret to those of us sitting just a few steps away.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must avoid a solution that merely shifts the problem. A professional fit-out addresses the financial waste, but without a strict usage policy, we will simply repeat the same patterns of imbalance and neglect. We need a structured purpose.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, structure is necessary, but let's ensure it includes a space for privacy. If we only focus on efficiency and rules, we'll continue to be strangers who can't speak honestly to one another when it truly matters.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm not interested in ""structures"" that just look good on paper. Whether it's a kitchen or a meeting room, someone always ends up doing the grunt work. Let's pick the option that requires the least amount of daily maintenance.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the option with the least maintenance is the one that actually works. A professional meeting space doesn't require scrubbing hobs. Let's stop the financial leak and invest in a purpose that serves the business.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that a room is more than its function; it is the air we breathe together. If we choose a path that ignores the noise and the mess, we only build a more expensive cage.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
